+ > **What this skill does and what it touches:** This skill helps agents guide users through BYOK setup on DeepRead. It calls `https://api.deepread.tech`, opens the DeepRead dashboard in the user's browser for key management, and may append `DEEPREAD_API_KEY` to a local `.env` file in the working directory if the device flow is run (only when the user explicitly opts in). It does not modify shell profiles or system-wide files. Required CLI tools: `curl`, `python3`.
+ ## Key Storage Best Practices
+ When the agent obtains your DeepRead API key via the device flow, it appends `DEEPREAD_API_KEY=...` to a local `.env` file in the working directory. Follow these practices to keep keys safe:
+ - **Add `.env` to your `.gitignore`** before running setup so the key never gets committed
+ - **Use scoped or test keys** when possible — most providers (OpenAI, Google) allow restricted-scope or short-lived keys for development
+ - **For production**, prefer a secrets manager (1Password CLI, OS keychain, AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault) over plaintext `.env`
+ - **Rotate keys regularly** and revoke unused ones at https://www.deepread.tech/dashboard
+ - **Never commit** `.env` files or share API keys in chat, screenshots, or logs
+ For provider keys (OpenAI/Google/OpenRouter), DeepRead validates them against the provider's API before encrypting and storing. Verify DeepRead's privacy policy and security practices at https://www.deepread.tech before submitting keys.